sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: From ChatGPT discovery to merchant checkout: an ACP product feed, a ChatGPT plugin, then external checkout or the payment sheet beta
  accDescr: Sequence diagram: From ChatGPT discovery to merchant checkout: an ACP product feed, a ChatGPT plugin, then external checkout or the payment sheet beta. 5 participants: Shopper, ChatGPT (agent surface), Merchant's ChatGPT plugin (MCP server and widget), Merchant (site, catalog and vault), and Merchant PSP and card rails. 13 steps, 10 crossing a trust boundary, 7 failure branches. Based on several protocols ACP 2026-04-17 OpenAI plugin checkout reference, formerly the Apps SDK monetization guide (read 2026-10-20) (2026-04-17). Step 1: Merchant (site, catalog and vault) to ChatGPT (agent surface): Push the product feed (ACP Feed API). This step crosses a trust boundary. If A feed file replaces the whole set with a partial file: Products missing from the file drop out the ACP file mode replaces the full product set. Step 2: Shopper to ChatGPT (agent surface): Ask for a product. Step 3: ChatGPT (agent surface) to Shopper: Show matching products from feeds. Step 4: ChatGPT (agent surface) to Merchant's ChatGPT plugin (MCP server and widget): Open the merchant's ChatGPT plugin (MCP tool call). This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 5: Merchant's ChatGPT plugin (MCP server and widget) to Shopper: Path A (generally available): link to the merchant's own checkout. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 6: Shopper to Merchant (site, catalog and vault): Path A: pay on the merchant's site. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 7: Merchant (site, catalog and vault) to Merchant PSP and card rails: Path A: authorize through the merchant's PSP. This step crosses a trust boundary. If The issuer declines: An ordinary decline on the merchant's site. Step 8: Merchant's ChatGPT plugin (MCP server and widget) to ChatGPT (agent surface): Path B (private beta): widget calls window.openai.requestCheckout. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 9: Shopper to ChatGPT (agent surface): Path B: choose a payment method and buy. If The shopper closes the sheet: No token is sent and nothing is charged. Step 10: ChatGPT (agent surface) to Merchant (site, catalog and vault): Path B, PCI DSS Level 1 merchants only: POST /agentic_commerce/delegate_payment. This step crosses a trust boundary. If Card data fails validation: Delegate Payment error invalid_card. If The same Idempotency-Key with a different body: idempotency_conflict. Step 11: Merchant (site, catalog and vault) to ChatGPT (agent surface): Path B, PCI DSS Level 1: 201 with a vault token id. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 12: ChatGPT (agent surface) to Merchant's ChatGPT plugin (MCP server and widget): Path B: complete_checkout tool call with a payment-method token. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 13: Merchant's ChatGPT plugin (MCP server and widget) to Merchant PSP and card rails: Path B: charge the token through a supported PSP. This step crosses a trust boundary. If A delegated token is used outside its allowance: Should fail, but ACP defines no error code for it the error is PSP specific. If The issuer declines: An ordinary decline the app tells the shopper.
  autonumber
  participant p_user as Shopper
  participant p_chatgpt as ChatGPT (agent surface)
  participant p_app as Merchant#39;s ChatGPT plugin (MCP server and widget)
  participant p_merchant as Merchant (site, catalog and vault)
  participant p_psp as Merchant PSP and card rails
  alt Expected path
    p_merchant->>p_chatgpt: Push the product feed (ACP Feed API)
    Note over p_merchant,p_chatgpt: Crosses a trust boundary
  else A feed file replaces the whole set with a partial file
    Note over p_merchant,p_chatgpt: Products missing from the file drop out#59; the<br/>ACP file mode replaces the full product set.
  end
  p_user->>p_chatgpt: Ask for a product
  p_chatgpt-->>p_user: Show matching products from feeds
  p_chatgpt->>p_app: Open the merchant#39;s ChatGPT plugin (MCP tool call)
  Note over p_chatgpt,p_app: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_app->>p_user: Path A (generally available): link<br/>to the merchant#39;s own checkout
  Note over p_app,p_user: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_user->>p_merchant: Path A: pay on the merchant#39;s site
  Note over p_user,p_merchant: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_merchant->>p_psp: Path A: authorize through the merchant#39;s PSP
    Note over p_merchant,p_psp: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The issuer declines
    Note over p_merchant,p_psp: An ordinary decline on the merchant#39;s site.
  end
  p_app->>p_chatgpt: Path B (private beta): widget calls<br/>window.openai.requestCheckout
  Note over p_app,p_chatgpt: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_user->>p_chatgpt: Path B: choose a payment method and buy
  else The shopper closes the sheet
    Note over p_user,p_chatgpt: No token is sent and nothing is charged.
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_chatgpt->>p_merchant: Path B, PCI DSS Level 1 merchants only#58;<br/>POST /agentic_commerce/delegate_payment
    Note over p_chatgpt,p_merchant: Crosses a trust boundary
  else Card data fails validation
    Note over p_chatgpt,p_merchant: Delegate Payment error invalid_card.
  else The same Idempotency-Key with a different body
    Note over p_chatgpt,p_merchant: idempotency_conflict.
  end
  p_merchant-->>p_chatgpt: Path B, PCI DSS Level 1: 201 with a vault token id
  Note over p_merchant,p_chatgpt: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_chatgpt->>p_app: Path B: complete_checkout tool<br/>call with a payment-method token
  Note over p_chatgpt,p_app: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_app->>p_psp: Path B: charge the token through a supported PSP
    Note over p_app,p_psp: Crosses a trust boundary
  else A delegated token is used outside its allowance
    Note over p_app,p_psp: Should fail, but ACP defines no error<br/>code for it#59; the error is PSP specific.
  else The issuer declines
    Note over p_app,p_psp: An ordinary decline#59; the app tells the shopper.
  end
